# Style Block {#title}

The `:::style` literal block embeds NODS rules. Its content is preserved as
literal text in the AST and emitted by the HTML renderer inside a `<style>`
element with break-out characters CSS-escaped.

:::style
h1 { color: #0f766e; }
p { line-height: 1.6; }
::: style

After-style paragraph remains a normal paragraph node.
